{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Infinite Power procs on casting damage-over-time spells, once per cast (#10806)",
  "contract": [
    "Infinite Power 92118 reads \"Casting damaging spells now reduces your damaging spell cooldowns by 10% of their",
    "remaining cooldown\". Its proc waited for the hit phase of a direct damage spell, so Unmake 804418, whose only damage",
    "is a periodic aura, never counted, while each tick of Melt Reality's triggered damage did: one cast cut a Timerend",
    "cooldown by about 36%. The proc now fires in the cast phase, once per cast of a non-triggered hostile spell, and",
    "spell_ascension_infinite_power keeps only spells that deal damage directly or periodically. Three talented",
    "Chronomancers start the same Timerend 801291 cooldown at the same moment (Timerend is itself a damaging cast, so",
    "all three get the same cut from it). One of them then casts nothing else and is the baseline; another casts Unmake",
    "and the third Melt Reality rank 7 572835. Each must end below the baseline by about 10% of a roughly 14 s",
    "remaining cooldown, more than 1 s, and Melt Reality by one proc only, not one per tick (under 2.2 s)."
  ],
